    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d368">

                <pb facs="0534" n="432" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg432"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2163: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-04-03T15:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 3, 1919,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received April 3,
                            2.20 p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>A memorandum from the Ministry for Foreign Affairs dated 2nd, while concurring in
                    principal with the suggestion made in your telegram of February 21st, 4
                        p.m.,<anchor n="87" xml:id="d368-f1"/> adds that:<anchor n="88"
                        xml:id="d368-f2"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Inasmuch, however, as England and France are deeply interested in this
                            question, it is deemed best that the proper course for the Imperial
                            Government to pursue before answering the American Government would be
                            to ascertain the opinions of the Governments of Great Britain and
                            France, to which nationalities the banking syndicate belongs.
                            Accordingly the necessary steps to this end have been taken.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d368-f1" n="87" xml:id="d368-f1-content">
                <p>See footnote 74, <ref target="#pg424">p. 424</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d368-f2" n="88" xml:id="d368-f2-content">
                <p>The original text of the memorandum is in Japanese; the excerpt in English was
                    received by the Department from the American Embassy in Tokyo.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
